Description: match key bindings by US key positions in non-Latin layouts
 Plain bindsym bindings match the keysyms of the active layout, so in a
 Russian, Greek or other non-Latin layout no letter binding (Mod4+z, ...)
 can match. GNOME handles this in mutter (needs_secondary_layout): when the
 active layout lacks one of the letters a-z on its first level, key bindings
 are also looked up in the US layout. Do the same here: when no binding
 matched and the key's layout lacks Latin letters, try the keysyms the key
 has on the first level of the US layout, with the raw modifiers.
 Layouts with Latin letters (us, de, fr, dvorak, ...) are not affected.
